1. Problem Statement
Analyze nested lists of environmental quality readings (e.g., Air Quality Index - AQI across multiple sampling stations over a week), calculate average and extreme (min/max) values, and classify ambient environmental safety levels against threshold standards.
2. Objectives
•	Process 2D environmental monitoring sensor matrices.
•	Calculate spatial and temporal average AQI levels.
•	Categorize pollution levels according to standard environmental safety indexes.
3. Assumptions
•	AQI values: 0-50 Good, 51-100 Moderate, 101-150 Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, >150 Unhealthy.
4. Algorithm
1. Read nested list matrix: Station rows with 7 daily AQI readings.
2. For each station, compute Mean, Min, and Max AQI.
3. Classify safety category based on station average.
4. Compute regional overall average.
5. Generate environmental audit summary.
